  "body": "Spec at <https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/rendering.html#tables-2:the-col-element> says:\r\n\r\n> The col element's width attribute maps to the dimension property (ignoring zero) 'width' on the col element.\r\n\r\nbut Gecko, WebKit, and Blink all allow 0.  Testcase:\r\n```\r\n<table style=\"display: block\">\r\n  <colgroup style=\"display: block\">\r\n    <col style=\"border: 1px solid green; display: block\" width=\"0\"></col>\r\n  </colgroup>\r\n</table>\r\n<script>\r\n  document.querySelector(\"col\").append(\"Text\");\r\n</script>\r\n```\r\nWe should align with implementations.\r\n\r\n@annevk ",
